ame":"On Me","artist":"Lil Baby","year":2021,"weight":4,"yt":"ieTnO1Dvt-I","src":"charts,singles","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":34094536844044,"name":"Billboard Year-End 2021","rank":36,"scaruffi":null},{"id":132335824845498,"name":"Billboard Year-End Hot 100","rank":36,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":219850022192911,"type":"song","name":"In a Minute","artist":"Lil Baby","year":2022,"weight":4,"yt":"4F_vcZ6KD9Q","src":"charts,singles","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":260042115848106,"name":"Billboard Year-End 2022","rank":43,"scaruffi":null},{"id":132335824845498,"name":"Billboard Year-End Hot 100","rank":43,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}}],"members":[],"member_of":[],"genres":[],"album_genres":[],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[{"id":109922206785763,"name":"Crunk y trap en Atlanta","book":"The Come Up: An Oral History of the Rise of Hip-Hop","author":"Jonathan Abrams","start":1997,"end":2020,"desc":"Lil Jon, A&R de So So Def, se convirtió con los East Side Boyz en la cara del crunk (Get Crunk, Who U Wit, 1997). En 1999 Def Jam ya no pudo ignorar el Sur y creó Def Jam South con Scarface al frente, que fichó a Chris Lova Lova, DJ de Hot 97.5 que vendía Incognegro desde el maletero: Ludacris (Back for the First Time, 2000). T.I., tras fracasar en Arista, se hizo fuerte con las mixtapes de DJ Drama, fundó Grand Hustle y con Trap Muzik (2003) llevó al gran público el trap, la música de la calle del trapicheo: sintetizadores, baterías potentes y charles nerviosos, con productores como DJ Toomp, Shawty Redd, Drumma Boy, Lex Luger o Zaytoven, cuyo piano hizo brillar a Gucci Mane (en un solo día de 2009 salieron «Bricks» y «Make Tha Trap Say Aye»). Luego Jeezy, Future, Migos, 21 Savage o Lil Baby: Atlanta, ciudad del fénix, destruye su sonido cada pocos años para crear otro.","color":"#f472b6","family":"El Sur: Miami, Atlanta, Houston, Memphis, Nueva Orleans","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/ComeUp/#trap"}],"